---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Implenix"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Implenix collects, uses, and protects personal information on implenix.net and in the course of providing medical billing services."
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy describes how Implenix ("Implenix," "we," "us," or
    "our") collects, uses, discloses, and protects information when you visit
    implenix.net (the "Site"), book a call with us, or engage us for medical
    billing services (the "Services").
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a patient of a healthcare practice that uses Implenix for
    billing, please note that we handle your health information on behalf of
    your provider as a business associate under HIPAA. That handling is
    governed by our agreement with your provider and by our
    <a href="/hipaa-notice">HIPAA Notice</a>, not solely by this policy. For
    questions about how your provider uses your health information, contact
    your provider directly.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you provide</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Booking and contact details.</strong> When you book a call or
      contact us, we collect your name, email address, phone number, practice
      name, specialty, and any notes you choose to share.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business information.</strong> If you become a client, we collect
      information needed to provide the Services, such as practice details,
      payer enrollment information, and billing records.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage data.</strong> Standard server logs may record your IP
      address, browser type, pages visited, and referring URLs. The Site is a
      static website and does not use third-party advertising trackers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To schedule and hold calls you book with us, including sending
      calendar invitations, meeting links, confirmations, and reminders.</li>
    <li>To provide, operate, and improve the Services.</li>
    <li>To respond to your inquiries and communicate with you about the
      Services.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our agreements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it with third
    parties for their own marketing purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we share information</h2>
  <p>We share information only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> that support our operations (for
      example, hosting, email delivery, and calendar scheduling), bound by
      confidentiality obligations and permitted to use the information only to
      provide services to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal authorities</strong> when required by law, subpoena, or
      other legal process, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of
      Implenix, our clients, or others.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A successor entity</strong> in connection with a merger,
      acquisition, or sale of assets, subject to this policy's commitments.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Protected health information (PHI)</h2>
  <p>
    In the course of providing billing services to healthcare practices, we
    receive and process protected health information as a business associate
    under HIPAA. We handle PHI in accordance with the Business Associate
    Agreements we sign with our clients and the safeguards described in our
    <a href="/hipaa-notice">HIPAA Notice</a>, including the minimum-necessary
    standard, access controls, and encryption in transit and at rest.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain booking and contact information for as long as needed to manage
    our relationship with you and as required by law. Billing records processed
    on behalf of clients are retained according to the terms of our client
    agreements and applicable healthcare record-retention requirements, after
    which they are securely deleted or returned.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We maintain administrative, technical, and physical safeguards appropriate
    to the sensitivity of the information we handle, including role-based
    access controls, encryption of data in transit, and workforce
    confidentiality obligations. No method of transmission or storage is
    completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal
      information we hold about you by emailing us at the address below.</li>
    <li>You may opt out of non-essential emails from us at any time by using
      the unsubscribe link in the email or by contacting us.</li>
    <li>Depending on your state of residence, you may have additional rights
      under state privacy laws. We will honor verified requests as required by
      applicable law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Site and Services are directed to businesses and healthcare
    professionals and are not intended for children under 13. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children through the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Effective" date
    above reflects the latest revision. Material changes will be posted on this
    page.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
  <address>
    <strong>Implenix</strong><br />
    1879 NW 8th St, Miami, FL 33125<br />
    <a href="mailto:contact@implenix.net">contact@implenix.net</a>
  </address>
</LegalLayout>
